Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||10-14-1999||06:35 PM||||I'm not using a flash and the sun is coming from the side. But I think it has something to do with the wavelength of red LEDs that is not picked up by the electronic thingy that controls shutter speed on my digital cam. I'll get out the ol' T70 and seen if I can shoot some better pictures.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||10-14-1999||07:10 PM||||It's hard to tell, but your dash "glass" is clear?<P>try "jelling" the dash, at least over the LEDs. If you know anyone in theatre then maybe you can borow some of the diferant red jell sheets. That would let you play with the contrast of the dash. Looks to me like the sunlight is hitting the matrix displays and making the contrast low. A jel/filter fould help that.<P>A sheet of polarizer would work real good for this.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-14-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eddie||10-14-1999||07:18 PM||||Cliff <BR>	A digital cam nice .OK I don't know alot about them but we have some nice ways to fix  up DIGITAL PICS if you would like to email them to me raw from your cam ill see if i can help you out.<BR>				EDDIE||||reg||14
Z||000010||Cliff Pennock||10-14-1999||07:32 PM||||Ogre, no the dash uses a special "signal red" front. It filters out every color except red. <P>Eddie, I can do the filtering too, but I especially didn't want to alter the picture digitally in any way... But lik I said, I'll get out the trusty T70 and shoot some better pictures.||||reg||1
